@startuml
title ClinicBook - Appointment state diagram (Fioralba Zika)

skinparam noteFontSize 11

state "Booked" as Booked
state "Cancelled" as Cancelled

[*] --> Booked : book (FR-03) [registered patient, free slot] / create appointment

Booked --> Cancelled : patient cancels [owner AND start in future AND at least 24 h before start] / status = Cancelled, slot released
Booked --> Cancelled : receptionist cancels [receptionist AND start in future] / status = Cancelled, slot released

Cancelled --> [*] : record retained; no further cancellation defined

note right of Booked
  Only BOOKED occupies a slot and counts towards the limit of 2 future bookings (FR-04, FR-05).
  A refused cancel request leaves the state unchanged: wrong owner, start not in future,
  or patient less than 24 h before start (FR-06, US-08, US-09).
end note

note left of Booked
  Time passing alone is not a cancellation event.
  No automatic attendance or no-show transition is drawn: the shared documents do not say
  who records those outcomes or when (open question).
end note

note right of Cancelled
  Terminal state of this modelled lifecycle, not deletion.
  Cancelled records are retained (proposed assumption) and the slot becomes free again.
  Exactly 24 h before start is still allowed for a patient cancel (proposed assumption).
end note

@enduml
